{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>Rejoice, O nations, with His people.</b> Then the nations will praise Israel, for they are the people of the Holy One, blessed be He, and they will say: Happy is the people that has it thus, that the Holy One, blessed be He, takes vengeance on their oppressors, as is explained further." "<b>For the blood of His servants He will avenge, and vengeance He will return to His adversaries.</b> That He will spill their blood as they spilled the blood of Israel. And thus it is written: ״יָדִין בַּגּוֹיִם מָלֵא גְוִיּוֹת״ — that the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to say to the nations: Why did you spill the blood of Israel? And they will want to deny having done so, and the Holy One, blessed be He, shows them His garments, which are full of corpses — meaning the holy bodies — and they will not be able to deny it. And then He will exact judgment from each one according to the judgment he did to Israel. And this is what the liturgical poet composed: 'התאזר בקדושים.' And likewise in the Akedah: 'אל דמי לדמי'; and also in the 'פורפירא מלא גויות.'" "<b>And He will atone His land, His people.</b> Israel are His people; He will atone His land — the Holy One's, blessed be He — as it is written: ״וְלָאָרֶץ לֹא יְכֻפַּר לַדָּם אֲשֶׁר שֻׁפַּךְ בָּהּ כִּי אִם בְּדַם שֹׁפְכוֹ״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:01.930039985Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}